A||||5||newfie||How does a water intercooler work?||||1||
Z||000000||newfie||11-21-2001||11:17 AM||||Wondering exactly how a water intercooler works??  Anyone know, are they better than the Air cooled?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||11-21-2001||12:25 PM||||water has a greater hea transport capability than air, so yes, in the aspect of removing heat, water is best. air-air is cheaper, and far more common.. but I do prefer air-water<P>I haven't got an air-water intercooler (or an air-air for that matter) but as far as I know.. the air flows through the intercooler, and instead of air flowing around it, there is water pumped around it. The water would then g through it's own radiator to dissipate that heat, unles it's a closed system with ice etc.. <P>if I'm mistaken, please feel free to correct me<P>------------------<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>     <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||11-21-2001||01:01 PM||||Darklord is correct.<P>air/Water intercoolers have their own cooling radiators with a pump circulating the water/coolant.  Air goes through the intercooler and gets cooled by the water/coolant.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||11-21-2001||04:21 PM||||I hate the machine at work, the keyboard hardly works.. trust me, I *can* spell "heat" and "go"..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||hugh||11-21-2001||05:40 PM||||Steve,You're right.Spearco says that a water to air intercooler will remove heat 9 times faster than air to air.||||reg||1
Z||000005||filthyscarecrow||11-21-2001||11:41 PM||||h2o intercoolers are more expensive though... that is... unless you make one. they're realy pretty easy to make. i'm using a stock DSM IC adn just welding new tanks on it for the air to go through (former frontal area) and then much smaller tanks for the water. i plan to run a heater core as the radiator for the IC (about the same size as the IC makes sure the rad is dissipating the heat from the water in the IC. <BR>the only major disadvantage of h20&gt;air is that after hard running, the water tends to get really hot after the car has been shut off and sitting. there is more heat soak into the water adn it takes longer to cool the water down again unless you use ice. remember, water has MUCh higher specific heat than air, so it takes more thermal energy to raise its temp, but that means it also takes much longer for it to dissipate that energy. i'm still conidering the air&gt;air. if anyone has done it successfully i'd love to see it, i just can't imagine how to get enough air flowing through that thing withou runnign intake pipes to the front of the car (can you say pressure drop?).||||reg||1
